    {
      "id": "tutorial-interface-save-refresh-trust-s5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Check yourself",
      "position": {
        "x": 930,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Check yourself",
        "body": "**Challenge**\n\n1. Make one visible change in a graph.\n2. State where that graph is saved.\n3. Save it deliberately.\n4. Refresh or reopen the graph.\n5. Explain why the result matches, or fails to match, your expectations.\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\nYou are done when you can say:\n- I know what save target I am editing\n- I know what refresh or reopen is expected to reload\n- I can distinguish transient UI state from persisted graph state\n- I have a recovery path when the graph seems wrong\n- trust comes from checking the source of truth, not guessing",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-interface-save-refresh-trust"
